<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nouméa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Port-de-France</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nouméa is the capital and largest city of New Caledonia, a French territory in the south-west Pacific. Founded in 1854 as the military post of Port-de-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, it was renamed in 1866 and grew as the administrative centre, the port of the penal colony and a nickel-processing town. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it was a major base for American forces in the Pacific.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/noumea.jpg" alt="Nouméa" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pilettes · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_over_Noumea.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
